-- title:
--   The semigroup $e^{t\mathcal L}$
-- statement:
--   For a linear superoperator $\mathcal L$ on the operators of the Fock space and $t\in\mathbb R$, $e^{t\mathcal L}=\sum_{k\ge0}t^k\mathcal L^k/k!$, the exponential of $t\mathcal L$ as an endomorphism of the finite-dimensional space of operators.
--
--   This is the evolution whose mixing time the main theorems bound.
--
--   **Formalization Note** It is computed as the matrix exponential of the matrix of $t\mathcal L$ in the basis of matrix units $|x\rangle\langle y|$; the exponential commutes with a change of basis.
-- source:
--   Bakshi, Moitra, Tan, Algorithmic Aspects of the Fermi–Hubbard Model, arXiv:2604.08408 (held version, sha256 055b8f8f…), Theorem 15.1, p.68

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FermiHubbardMix_parityOp
open scoped BigOperators
open Matrix
noncomputable section

namespace FermiHubbardMix

/-- The semigroup `e^{tL}` generated by a linear superoperator `L` on the Fock-space operators
(arXiv:2604.08408, held version sha256 055b8f8f…, Theorem 15.1, p.68).

**Formalization Note** `e^{tL}` is the exponential of the matrix of `t·L` in the basis of matrix
units `|x⟩⟨y|`, mapped back to a linear map. The exponential commutes with change of basis, so this
is the exponential of `t·L` as an endomorphism of the finite-dimensional space of operators. -/
def semigroup {N : ℕ} (L : Op N →ₗ[ℂ] Op N) (t : ℝ) : Op N →ₗ[ℂ] Op N :=
  Matrix.toLin (Matrix.stdBasis ℂ (Fin N → Fin 2) (Fin N → Fin 2))
    (Matrix.stdBasis ℂ (Fin N → Fin 2) (Fin N → Fin 2))
    (NormedSpace.exp ((t : ℂ) • LinearMap.toMatrix (Matrix.stdBasis ℂ (Fin N → Fin 2) (Fin N → Fin 2))
      (Matrix.stdBasis ℂ (Fin N → Fin 2) (Fin N → Fin 2)) L))

end FermiHubbardMix


